This code uses the pigpio library for SPI communication with the MCP3008 analog-to-digital converter. It initializes the GPIO pins, sets up the ADC channel, opens the SPI device, and starts reading ADC values. The code then calculates the moisture trend and logs the timestamp and moisture trend to the console. It also handles sleep intervals of 1 second between each ADC value read and calculates the ADC value's percentage of full scale.

The program also includes error handling for SPI initialization and every SPI transfer, reporting any failure rather than silently continuing. It also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM for graceful shutdown, making sure the SPI handle is closed and pigpio is terminated cleanly on every exit path, including early failures.

