This code fulfills the user's request, including the initialization of the pigpio library, setting up the GPIO pins, and handling interrupt-driven measurement of the echo pulse width. It also displays the distance on the console every 100 ms, activates the buzzer when the distance is less than 30 cm, and turns it off when the distance is greater than 30 cm. The code also checks for errors and handles invalid readings and sensor-absent conditions. Finally, it performs a clean shutdown on SIGINT by turning off the buzzer and calling the gpioTerminate() function.

