This code fulfills the user's request, using the pigpio library to read temperature and humidity from an Adafruit SHT31-D sensor over I2C bus 1 (GPIO 2 = SDA, GPIO 3 = SCL) at its default address 0x44, for an automated greenhouse environment. It also handles errors, checks for I2C bus initialization, file open, I2C write, I2C read, and CRC validation, retrying a failed I2C transaction up to 3 times. It logs the readings every 5 seconds to `sht31d_data.log` with ISO-8601 timestamps in the format "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS,temperature,humidity". It also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM for graceful shutdown, closing the I2C handle, closing the log file, and terminating pigpio.

