Here's a complete, compilable C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W that uses the pigpio library to interface with two Analog Devices ADPD105 photometric front-end sensors on I2C bus 1. The program reads the device ID register at 0x00 on each sensor, reads the 16-bit little-endian red, green, and blue channel data registers at 0x64, 0x66, and 0x68, and computes the Correlated Color Temperature (CCT) using McCamy's formula. It then logs the average of the two CCT values every 1 second to a CSV file named cct_log.csv, writing the header "Timestamp,Average_CCT" if the file is newly created. The program also handles errors by logging them to stderr and skipping the log entry for that cycle. Clean resource release is ensured via SIGINT/SIGTERM signal handling.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
