Here's a complete, compilable C program for a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ using the pigpio library and a hardware timer interrupt to sample a single BMP180 pressure sensor over I2C bus 1 at address 0x77. The program validates the calibration data read from registers 0xAA-0xBF before starting measurements, then uses oversampling setting 0 (ultra low power) to log temperature (°C) and pressure (Pa) readings to bmp180_log.txt every 500 ms. It also implements robust error handling for I2C communication failures, sensor absent, bus errors, and read/write timeouts, and ensures clean resource release on all exit paths via signal handling for SIGINT and SIGTERM.

