This code fulfills the user's request by toggling data logging from a BMP180 pressure sensor at I2C address 0x77 to a file named "pressure_log.txt", with each logged line recording a timestamp together with the pressure reading in Pa. The toggle is driven by falling-edge detection on GPIO27, debounced with a 200 ms window so repeated edges from a single press are not counted twice. At startup and periodically thereafter, read the BMP180's calibration data and use it with the Bosch compensation formulas to compute pressure from the raw sensor bytes, writing a new log line every 2 seconds for as long as logging remains enabled. The code also handles I2C communication errors, as well as pigpio library initialization failures without crashing the program. On receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM, clean up all open resources, including the I2C handle and the pigpio library instance, before the process exits.

