This code uses the libgpiod API to sample the analog audio output of an Adafruit MAX9814 Electret Microphone Amplifier, connects the MAX9814 OUT pin to GPIO 17 (configured as input), and sets GPIO 18 LOW to select 60dB gain. It also handles errors, checks for rising edges (logic HIGH) as peak sound events, and logs each detected peak to the audio_log.txt file with a timestamp formatted as 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS LEVEL'. The code also ensures clean release of all libgpiod resources on all exit paths via SIGINT/SIGTERM signal handling.

