Here's a complete, compilable C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B using the pigpio library to monitor a SainSmart IR Flame Sensor Module (LM393 comparator, IR photodiode) connected to GPIO 4 (digital DO pin), which outputs LOW when a flame is detected and HIGH when no flame is present. The program polls the sensor every 50 ms with 50 ms software debouncing, and when a flame is detected, it drives a PWM-controlled cooling fan on GPIO 18 using hardware PWM at 100 Hz, scaling the duty cycle from 0 to 80% based on flame duration using an exponential curve. It also logs all events (system start, flame detected, flame ended, shutdown) with ISO-8601 timestamps to 'flame_log.txt'. The program implements robust error handling, checks for every GPIO read, handles sensor-absent conditions with a timeout, and cleanly releases all resources on SIGINT/SIGTERM.

