This program opens the I2C bus, sets the I2C address to 0x23, and sets the One-Time High-Resolution Mode 2 command (0x21). It then waits for the maximum conversion time of 180 ms, reads 2 bytes of data, calculates the illuminance in lux, and logs the sensor readings to 'light_log.txt'. The program also handles potential I2C write/read errors and sensor-absent paths.

To compile and run the program, use the following commands:

```
gcc -o i2c_sensor i2c_sensor.c -lgpiod -lpigpio
./i2c_sensor
```

This will create a 'light_log.txt' file in the same directory as the compiled program, logging the illuminance readings from the BH1750FVI light sensor.

