This code initializes the pigpio library, sets up the GPIO pins, and handles button presses. It also de-energizes the coils after each rotation and prints console messages for lock and unlock actions.

To compile and run the code, use the following commands:

```bash
gcc -o door_lock door_lock.c -lpigpio -lrt
./door_lock
```

This code assumes that the L293D motor driver is connected to GPIO 4, GPIO 17, GPIO 27, and GPIO 22 (mapped to BCM GPIOs 24, 23, 22, and 17, respectively). Make sure to adjust the GPIO numbers if your setup is different.

